WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:09.357
This video shows where the trigger of an animation lives. It is part of the file, set here in the editor, and every player follows it.

2
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.792
The trigger is in the settings of the document. Let's scroll down to it.

3
00:00:16.533 --> 00:00:21.836
Start is set to on load, so the animation plays as soon as it is on the page.

4
00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:27.220
Let's make it start on mouse over instead, and open the preview to try it.

5
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:36.238
The preview plays the file exactly as a player would. Nothing moves, because it waits for the pointer.

6
00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:39.818
Let's point at it, and then move away.

7
00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:48.600
It plays while the pointer is over it, and pauses when the pointer leaves.

8
00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:54.300
A click can start it too. Let's switch the start to on click.

9
00:00:56.967 --> 00:01:00.545
Now a click starts it, and the next click pauses it.

10
00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:03.099
Let's click it twice.

11
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.635
The first click plays it, and the second one pauses it.

12
00:01:11.867 --> 00:01:20.200
So, the trigger is part of the file. Set it once in the editor, and every player and every export starts the same way.
